    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1052">

                <pb facs="1230" n="1034" sameAs="frus:frus1945Berlinv02/pg1034"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 Potsdam/8–145</note>
                <head>No. 1052<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Proposal by the British
                        Delegation</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d1052-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Babelsberg</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-08-01">August 1, 1945</date>.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Note</hi></p>
                <p>It was agreed<anchor n="2" xml:id="d1052-f2"/> that the British and American
                    Commanders would provide 40,000 tons of food a month and 2,400 tons of coal a
                    day for the British and American Zones in Berlin for thirty days running from
                    July 15th. Pending the establishment of an agreement for the instalments of
                    commodities to be made available by the Soviet Government under paragraph 4 (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">a</hi>) of the Reparations Agreement,<anchor n="3"
                        xml:id="d1052-f3"/> the Control Council should be instructed to draw up
                    immediately a programme of the food, coal and fuel which will need to be
                    imported during the next six months into the Greater Berlin area to bring the
                    standard of the whole of the population of that area up to an agreed level.
                    These amounts will be furnished by the Soviet Government to the Greater Berlin
                    area as an advance delivery under paragraph 4 (<hi rendition="#italic">a</hi>)
                    of the Reparations Agreement.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
